{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774301207,"nonce":"pXLxeVpqKxhhORWYM3IO5sAnOfc=","message":"**Implementation spec — frontend run selector**\n\n**New files:**\n- `web/src/types/runs.ts` — TypeScript interfaces: `TrainingRun`, `EvalRun`, with id, name, timestamp, status, hyperparameters metadata\n- `web/src/stores/runStore.ts` — Zustand store: `selectedTrainingRunId`, `selectedEvalRunId`, lists of runs (stub data initially), select/create actions\n- `web/src/api/runAPI.ts` — Stub API calls: `fetchTrainingRuns()`, `fetchEvalRuns(trainingRunId)`, `createTrainingRun()` — return mock data, ready for backend wiring\n- `web/src/components/panels/RunSelector.tsx` — Two-level dropdown widget: training run selector (left) + eval run selector (right). Compact pill style matching existing tab buttons. Shows run name + timestamp. \"New Run\" button only visible on Training tab.\n\n**Modified files:**\n- `web/src/components/layout/BottomShelf.tsx` — RunSelector placed in the header bar, right of tab pills, shared across all tabs. Passes `activeTab` so RunSelector can conditionally show \"New Run.\"\n- `web/src/components/panels/TrainingPanel.tsx` — No direct integration needed; RunSelector is in BottomShelf header.\n\n**Design decisions:**\n- RunSelector lives in BottomShelf header (not per-panel) so state is visually shared across tabs\n- Zustand store (not React context) for consistency with existing patterns (trainingStore, graphStore, etc.)\n- Stub data with 2 mock training runs and 2 eval runs each, so the UI is testable before backend exists\n- Compact inline style (pill dropdowns) matching existing tab button aesthetics","files":null}]}